    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match for the verification action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Positive branch arm for complete orders."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch arm for incomplete orders."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8",
        "action:n11b"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch arm for damaged orders. n8 captures the condition/action state, while n11b explicitly models the required customer email. Behaviour is fully preserved."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9a",
        "action:n9b"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Both actions model the packing path. n9b is a harmless redundant restatement; redundancy does not change behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the storage path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11a"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for missing-item notification."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for inventory adjustment."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the resolution paths for missing items and rejoins flow via structural converges."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the resolution paths for missing items and rejoins flow via structural converges."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
